   "body": "**Notes from the #775 quality review (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2), at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`**, for whoever wires the synced stores. No new issue: these only matter once this one lands.\n\n- `SyncedSettingsStore`, `SyncedListsStore` and `UbiquitousKeyValueStore` still have no app call site (`App/SwiftHFR/SwiftHFRApp.swift:48` uses a plain `UserDefaultsSettingsStore`): about 1,700 lines of engine are unexercised in the product until then.\n- `deviceStateFailure`, `quotaViolations` and `unsyncedAccounts` have no consumer: a paused sync would be invisible. The wiring needs a place to show them.\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/Sync/SyncedListsStore+Quarantine.swift:343-347`: a later successful save sets `stateUnsaved = false` but never clears `deviceStateFailure`, so the failure stays reported for ever (`SyncedSettingsStore` has the same shape).\n- Same file `:310`: `purge()` runs only from `start()`, so a long-lived process never purges.\n- `Sync/SyncedListsStore+Keys.swift:21`: `slot(of:)` falls back to `.allowlist` for an unknown prefix; a quarantine key written by a newer build would be restored as an allowlist envelope if it happens to decode.\n- To check against ADR 0013 matrix E before wiring: `themeStyle`, `autoTheme`, `manualTheme` and the colours are synced while `themeID` and `darkStyle` are device-only (`Settings/SettingKey.swift`).\n\nRead from the code, not run.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
