   "body": "**cloud/m4q-reliab-opus, a note for whoever wires `SyncedListsStore` (found while working on #1182, PR #1240):**\n\n#1240 lets the member discard an unreadable local store (`discardUnreadableData()`: the file goes to `.corrupt` and the store starts empty). Today the app does not run `SyncedListsStore`, so nothing is pushed.\n\nOnce it runs, a discarded synced list (allowlist, super-favourites, smiley favourites, rehost history) is empty next to the device's digest of the last synced list. `reconcile` (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/Sync/SyncedListsStore+Lists.swift:39`) then takes it for a change made here and pushes the empty list, wiping it on every device.\n\nThe wiring should make a discard drop that slot's digests (so the cloud copy replaces the empty local one), with a test: unreadable local store, cloud holding a list, discard → the cloud list comes back, nothing pushed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
